            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0508" n="420" xml:id="pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/828: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-24T10:00:00-02:00">January 24, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 24—8:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9. Although Colombian flotilla is only 4 days distance from Leticia, Peru’s
                    attitude remains unaltered. As Brazil desires to leave no means unemployed for
                    maintaining continental peace, she proposes to circularize tomorrow all the
                    American powers requesting them to make representations in Lima individually for
                    maintenance thereof.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph today whether you approve Brazil’s intention.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Lima.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
